'''''Carex peregrina''''' is a species of [[Carex|sedge]] (family [[Cyperaceae]]), with a remarkably disjunct distribution; it is found in the [[Azores]] and [[Madeira]] islands in the eastern Atlantic, and more than {{cvt|6000|km|mi}} away in the mountains of Ethiopia, Kenya, Uganda and Tanzania, in east Africa.<ref name="POWO_301507-1" >{{cite POWO |id=301507-1 |title=''Carex peregrina'' Link |access-date=5 October 2022 |quote=[[Bale Mountains]] ... [[Mount Meru (Tanzania)|Mt. Meru]] }}</ref> It prefers to grow in montane forests but occasionally is found sunny [[grassland]]s from {{cvt|2300|to|3500|m}} above sea level.<ref name="1_of_42_Google_Scholar_Hits" >{{cite journal |title=Synopsis of ''Carex'' (Cyperaceae) from sub-Saharan Africa and Madagascar |year=2011 |last1=Gehrke |first1=Berit |journal=Botanical Journal of the Linnean Society |volume=166 |pages=51–99 |doi=10.1111/j.1095-8339.2011.01116.x |doi-access=free }}</ref>

